{"nodes": [{"id": "booking_Booking", "label": "Booking Aggregate", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "booking_Booking", "label": "Booking (aggregate root)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All state mutation goes through intention-revealing methods (Confirm/Cancel/Complete/MarkNoShow) with private setters, so the status state machine and the cancellation window cannot be bypassed by callers."}, {"id": "booking_StatusTransitionInvariants", "label": "Booking status transition invariants (guarded state machine)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every mutator re-checks the current status and throws InvalidOperationException rather than silently no-op'ing, so illegal transitions surface as errors. Legal edges: Create->Pending; Pending->Confirmed; Confirmed->Completed; Confirmed->NoShow; Pending|NoShow->Cancelled. Completed and Cancelled are terminal. Note the asymmetry: NoShow is reachable but is not blocked from Cancel, and no transition exists out of NoShow otherwise."}, {"id": "booking_CancellationWindowInvariant", "label": "Two-hour cancellation cutoff invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cancel() refuses when Slot.StartDateTime minus UtcNow is under 2 hours, protecting the staff member's held time. The rule is hard-coded in the aggregate (not configurable) and, because the subtraction is signed, it also blocks cancelling any booking whose start time has already passed."}, {"id": "booking_LoyaltyPointsAward", "label": "Flat 10-point award on booking completion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Complete() hard-codes LoyaltyPointsEarned = 10 \u2014 a flat per-visit award, independent of SalonService.Price or DurationMinutes. The Booking only records the amount and publishes it; it never touches Customer.LoyaltyPoints itself, so the actual credit must happen in a BookingCompleted handler outside the domain layer."}, {"id": "booking_AggregateRootPattern", "label": "DDD aggregate root vs child entity split", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Booking, Customer and SalonService derive from AggregateRoot (and so are the only types IRepository<T> accepts); LoyaltyTransaction and Notification derive from Entity and are reached through their owner or a bespoke repository."}, {"id": "booking_AggregateReferenceById", "label": "Cross-aggregate references held as bare Guids", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Booking stores CustomerId/StaffId/ServiceId (and LoyaltyTransaction/Notification store CustomerId/BookingId) as plain Guids with no navigation properties, keeping each aggregate independently loadable and transactionally separate. The cost is that no referential invariant is enforced inside the domain."}, {"id": "booking_EfCorePrivateConstructor", "label": "Private parameterless constructor for EF Core materialization", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each persisted class exposes only a static factory plus a private ctor (commented `// EF Core` on Booking) so ORM rehydration works without opening a public constructor that would let callers build invalid state."}, {"id": "booking_Booking", "label": "Booking aggregate root", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "booking_booking", "label": "Booking (aggregate root)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "booking_Booking", "target": "bookingcreated_BookingCreated", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "booking_Booking", "target": "bookingconfirmed_BookingConfirmed", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "booking_Booking", "target": "bookingcancelled_BookingCancelled", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "booking_Booking", "target": "bookingcompleted_BookingCompleted", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/SpaReservation.Domain/Bookings/Booking.cs", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "booking_Booking", "target": "bookingslot_BookingSlot", "relation": 